<title>USA: Wall Street stocks lower at start.</title>
<headline>Wall Street stocks lower at start.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dow industrials were down in early trading, falling prey to profit-taking after yesterday's rally to their first record close in nearly two months.</p>
<p>--Dow Industrials .DJI off 12 at 7203.</p>
<p>--Nasdaq Composite .IXIC off six at 1333.</p>
<p>--S&amp;P Index .SPX off two at 829.</p>
<p>--NYSE advance/decline .AD.N 109/254</p>
<p>--Nasdaq advance/decline .AD.O 548/669</p>
<p>--The 30-year long bond off 15/32 to yield 6.92 percent.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1737))</p>
</text>
